      "title": "Held in Trust",
      "text": "Under a pane of clouded glass lies a girl of nine, breathing slow as winter. Flour still dusts one sleeve.\n\nA brass plate on the lid: I. BRANNOCK. HELD IN TRUST UNTIL SAFE.\n\nSeventeen years, and she has not aged a day. Her lips move in her sleep, shaping the same word over and over, the way you repeat a thing so as not to forget it.\n\nThe word is \"Marta\".",
