      "text": "Hush, little names, the ink is deep,\nthe Hunger walks but cannot keep\nwhat no one speaks and no one knows.\nSleep in the ledger. Sleep in the snows.\n\nHush, little names, till morning comes,\ntill someone signs the Seal for sums\nof all the souls we hid below.\nUntil then, sleep. And I will not go.\n\nIn the margin, in a shaking hand: \"Morning never comes. The Chief Archivist went mad. I sing anyway.\""
